																		Site Crit - Rieview
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/riemann" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1787775); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1787775&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238082" alt="Riemann" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1787775)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/riemann" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1787775); return false;" >Riemann</a></span> <span class="odate time_1599949544 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">12 Sep 2020 22:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4773441">
									

<p>Oh boy, I'm going to get some <em>responses</em> from <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-kirby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3440103); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3440103&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1599949544" alt="Captain Kirby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3440103)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-kirby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3440103); return false;">Captain Kirby</a></span> about this.</p>
<p>When I was asked to look this over, I knew one thing about the article. People don't die anymore. I'm a EoD neophyte and that's the angle that I approached this from.</p>
<p>I am both pleased and disappointed to say that this is another banger from CaptainKirby. There's a good sense of place, with well realised characters with motivations that make sense and drive their actions. The exploration is very strong, but for me, never quite passes the line of fantastic, largely because of the thematic reasons I'll get to in a minute. I'm sure this is quite the excellent epilogue to the good work that Kirbs has been putting out for the rest of the EoD canon, but&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I don't think that the framing device of a park justifies itself thematically <em>or</em> format-ly. For an article that is ultimately supposed to be an exploration of the crushing sense of ennui that comes from eternal life, the concept of this park as a natural consequence of trying to escape aforementioned ennui falls surprisingly flat.</p>
<p>I think this is largely because the actual park is&#8230; weirdly mundane? It gets weirder towards the end, but a solid 70% of the article is a fairly straightforward reinterpretation of common ideas of the afterlife - heaven, Valhalla, hell&#8230; but there's no real sense of interaction with these ideas or themes that feel, to me, particularly unique.</p>
<p>So rather than having a park that feels like the endstate of a deathless society and the initial exploration being an allegory for those feelings, only for us to know that it's ultimately been commodified into a theme park, we get&#8230;</p>
<p>A story that <em>happens</em> to take place in this weird area. And then that area happens to be turned into a park for reasons that feel wholly unrelated to the themes as a whole. And I think there's a version of this that works so much better, and I know Captain Kirby is more than capable of writing it.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I've been accused of being a grouchy purist - I like my format screws to be justified. I don't think this does that, but moreover I think the format screw takes away from the themes in the article, and as such, I'm going to no-vote this one.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:smaller;"><em>These opinions do not reflect any official staff position and are only my thoughts. Please contact Site Crit Team Captain <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1599949544" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;">SoullessSingularity</a></span> with any complaints.</em></span></p>

							</div>

								
					
